  "body": "In **X(HT)ML**, the following:\r\n```xhtml\r\n<p>\r\n  <p>Paragraph 1</p>\r\n  <p>Paragraph 2</p>\r\n</p>\r\n```\r\nResults in the following DOM:\r\n```html\r\n └<p>\r\n   ├<p>\r\n   │ └ #text: Paragraph 1\r\n   └<p>\r\n     └ #text: Paragraph 2\r\n```\r\nBut in **HTML**, it currently results in a different, unintuitive DOM:\r\n```html\r\n ├<p>\r\n ├<p>\r\n │ └ #text: Paragraph 1\r\n ├<p>\r\n │ └ #text: Paragraph 2\r\n └<p>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI’d like if there was a way for nested `<p>` tags to work in HTML without breaking backwards compatibility.\r\n\r\nA way to support that might be if all `<p>` tags would be properly closed using `</p>`, thus forming a balanced tree.",
